// sql-injection-reviewed-file: disposable-cluster TEST HARNESS (database layer), never request-path code. Every DDL interpolation is an identifier generated by this harness (`fbc_<tag>_<run>`) passed through ident(), which accepts only ^[a-z_][a-z0-9_]{0,62}$ and double-quotes it; passwords go only as $n bind parameters or through format('%L') inside a DO block reading a transaction-local setting. Reviewed 2026-11-19 (provider-neutral db-setup).
/**
 * Owner decision 2026-11-19 (provider-neutral db-setup; option 1 "Create login, you set password"): the real-database proof of
 * the capability-based behaviour of the bootstrap child. Run by run-fallback-check.sh on a docker host (InstaBox), never
 * against a real provider:
 *
 *   FBC_PLAIN_SU_URL   the superuser of a plain PostgreSQL 16 with TLS (server certificate for 127.0.0.1 from FBC's CA)
 *   FBC_SIM_SU_URL     the superuser of a PostgreSQL 16 with TLS that loads refuse_prehashed.c: it refuses pre-hashed role
 *                      passwords at COMMIT (XX000); switched by SIGHUP settings it also refuses a plain-text password
 *                      (refuse_prehashed.refuse_plain), a role created without a password (refuse_passwordless_role), or a
 *                      pre-hashed password inside the statement instead of at COMMIT (refuse_at_statement). Its logging is
 *                      the N4 setting: log_statement = ddl, log_min_error_statement = error, log_lock_waits = on,
 *                      deadlock_timeout = 100ms, log_min_duration_statement = -1
 *   FBC_BOUNCER1_HOSTPORT / FBC_BOUNCER2_HOSTPORT   PgBouncer (transaction pooling) in front of the plain cluster: 1 with
 *                      its defaults (refuses the startup option db-setup sends), 2 with ignore_startup_parameters=options
 *   PG_SSL_CA_CERT_PATH  the CA of both clusters (handed to the child)
 *   FBC_SIM_CONTAINER  docker container name: its log is searched for the crewflow_owner password
 *
 * Scenarios (each from a clean cluster state; crewflow_owner is cluster-wide). Fixed lines are asserted through
 * OWNER_BOOTSTRAP_MESSAGES itself, never copied strings:
 *   P1  plain PG16, verify-full, a non-superuser CREATEROLE admin: the pre-hashed path; created, the login works.
 *   P2  plain PG16, the cluster superuser as the admin over verify-full (the bundled db's mode a): the same.
 *   N1  the refusing server over verified TLS (owner decision 2026-11-20): ONE run, 0. The verifier is refused at COMMIT,
 *       TWICE (security review F5 of #266: verifierRefused, verifierRetry, then the plain line, in that order; two
 *       pre-hashed refusals in the server log), then db-setup sets the same password in plain text (plainFallbackUsed + plainFallbackLogsNotice, result plainText);
 *       crewflow_owner LOGIN, the PG_DATABASE_URL password logs in, a wrong one does not, pg_authid stores SCRAM-SHA-256$.
 *       The password is in no child output line (nor in this cluster's ddl-level server log).
 *       No plainFallbackTlsEndsAtProxy line (TLS ends at the server itself; the proxy case is covered by the unit tests).
 *   N1b the same server WITHOUT verified TLS, twice: sslmode=disable (no TLS), and sslmode=require with
 *       PG_SSL_ALLOW_SELF_SIGNED=true (TLS, certificate not verified): plainFallbackNoVerifiedTls, the last resort
 *       (passwordless NOLOGIN crewflow_owner + the printed step), 64; nothing logs in.
 *   N2a the server also refuses the plain form (refuse_plain): plainFallbackRefused, then the passwordless NOLOGIN role + the
 *       printed step (64); a second run writes nothing and repeats it (no loop); the operator's step (the printed statements
 *       typed LITERALLY: the DO block alone refused cleanly, a value the server refuses, then the real value; refuse_plain
 *       switched off for it: the simulator cannot tell a provider's own console from db-setup); the next run continues, 0.
 *   N2b refuse_plain AND refuse_passwordless_role: nothing created, the reviewed manual-role SQL printed (64); the operator
 *       runs it (refuse_plain off, as in N2a); the next run continues, 0.
 *   N3  an existing crewflow_owner whose password is not the one in PG_DATABASE_URL: without the opt-in 64 passwordMismatch,
 *       unchanged; CREWFLOW_ROTATE_APP_PASSWORD=yes 64 rotateInvalidValue, unchanged; =1 set (through the plain fallback on
 *       this server) with rotateDone, 0; =1 again rotateNothingToDo, 0.
 *   N4  logging leak check: a successful plain set (as N1), then a plain set that FAILS inside its role statement (the
 *       verifier refused at the statement, refuse_at_statement; another session holds the crewflow_owner row, so the
 *       plain ALTER ROLE waits and lock_timeout fires, 55P03, before log_lock_waits at deadlock_timeout could quote it). The
 *       server log and the child output hold neither value, and no log_lock_waits line was written (security review F10).
 *       Then, recorded and NOT asserted: what log_statement = all (set for the admin role) writes: the documented
 *       "provider logs" trade-off (plainFallbackLogsNotice).
 *   N5  PostgreSQL 17+ only (skipped with a note on 16): N4 (B) with a DATABASE-level transaction_timeout = 100ms and
 *       deadlock_timeout = 1s, so lock_timeout (500ms) would come AFTER the transaction timeout's FATAL (which would carry
 *       the formatted role statement as CONTEXT): db-setup's P0 guard (review F2) turns the session's transaction_timeout
 *       off before the plain set, so it fails cleanly on lock_timeout (55P03), no FATAL, no value in the server log.
 *   Q1  role squatting (independent review L2): crewflow_owner already exists and another role is a member of it: refused
 *       (64) before anything is written.
 *   H1  the printed admin-grant hint (owner SQL review): a plain WITH ADMIN OPTION is refused as another member; the hint,
 *       run as written, lets db-setup set the password (0). Every run carries CREWFLOW_ROTATE_APP_PASSWORD=1: since owner
 *       decision 2026-11-20 an existing password is changed only with that opt-in (rotateDone on the last run).
 *   T1  a PostgreSQL 16 whose pg_hba TRUSTS crewflow_owner (FBC_TRUST_SU_URL): db-setup creates crewflow_owner, then its
 *       deliberately-wrong-password login succeeds, so it refuses (64) with "the server lets crewflow_owner log in WITHOUT
 *       its password"; the second run refuses before any write. (Security re-review R1 of #259.)
 * Output: scenario ids, PASS / FAIL, never a value.
 */
import { execFileSync, spawn } from 'node:child_process';
import { randomBytes } from 'node:crypto';
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { join, resolve } from 'node:path';

import { Client } from 'pg';

import { OWNER_BOOTSTRAP_MESSAGES, OWNER_BOOTSTRAP_RESULT_PREFIX, OWNER_SQL_BEGIN_MARKER, OWNER_SQL_END_MARKER, OwnerBootstrapResult } from '../owner-bootstrap';
import { OWNER_AWAITING_PASSWORD_MARK, OWNER_MANUAL_ROLE_SQL, OWNER_SET_PASSWORD_SQL } from '../owner-bootstrap-sql';

/** A printed operator statement with its placeholder replaced LITERALLY by `value` (what the operator types). */
const typed = (statement: string, value: string): string => statement.split('<PG_DATABASE_APP_PASSWORD>').join(value);

const REPO_ROOT = resolve(__dirname, '..', '..', '..', '..', '..', '..', '..', '..');
const TSCONFIG_APP = join(REPO_ROOT, 'packages', 'rab-server', 'tsconfig.app.json');
const ENTRY = join(__dirname, '..', 'bootstrap-owner-login.ts');
const RUN = `${Date.now().toString(36)}${randomBytes(2).toString('hex')}`;
const SECRETS = new Set<string>();
const remember = (v: string): string => {
  SECRETS.add(v);
  return v;
};
const log = (m: string) => process.stdout.write(`[fallback-check] ${m}\n`);

class Failed extends Error {}
function expect(cond: unknown, what: string): void {
  if (!cond) throw new Failed(what);
}

function need(name: string): string {
  const v = process.env[name];
  if (!v) throw new Error(`${name} is required`);
  return v;
}

const CA_PATH = need('PG_SSL_CA_CERT_PATH');
const CA = readFileSync(CA_PATH, 'utf8');
/** The runner starts one PostgreSQL at a time (the laptop's memory rule), so each cluster URL is optional per run. */
const optionalCluster = (name: string): URL | null => {
  const v = process.env[name];
  if (!v) return null;
  const u = new URL(v);
  if (u.hostname !== '127.0.0.1') throw new Error('loopback disposable clusters only');
  remember(decodeURIComponent(u.password));
  return u;
};
const PLAIN_OR_NULL = optionalCluster('FBC_PLAIN_SU_URL');
const SIM_OR_NULL = optionalCluster('FBC_SIM_SU_URL');
const TRUST_OR_NULL = optionalCluster('FBC_TRUST_SU_URL');
const cluster = (u: URL | null, name: string): URL => {
  if (!u) throw new Failed(`${name} is not set for this run`);
  return u;
};
// Accessed lazily by each scenario (a scenario of another group never touches an unset cluster).
const clusters = {
  get PLAIN() {
    return cluster(PLAIN_OR_NULL, 'FBC_PLAIN_SU_URL');
  },
  get SIM() {
    return cluster(SIM_OR_NULL, 'FBC_SIM_SU_URL');
  },
  get TRUST() {
    return cluster(TRUST_OR_NULL, 'FBC_TRUST_SU_URL');
  },
};

function ident(name: string): string {
  if (!/^[a-z_][a-z0-9_]{0,62}$/.test(name)) throw new Error('not a plain identifier');
  return `"${name}"`;
}

function urlFor(base: URL, user: string, password: string, db: string, query = 'sslmode=verify-full', hostport?: string): string {
  const u = new URL(base.toString());
  if (hostport) u.host = hostport;
  u.username = user;
  u.password = encodeURIComponent(password);
  u.pathname = `/${db}`;
  u.search = query;
  return remember(u.toString());
}

async function sql(base: URL, db: string, text: string, values: unknown[] = []): Promise<Record<string, unknown>[]> {
  const c = new Client({
    host: base.hostname,
    port: Number(base.port),
    user: decodeURIComponent(base.username),
    password: decodeURIComponent(base.password),
    database: db,
    ssl: { ca: CA, rejectUnauthorized: true },
  });
  await c.connect();
  try {
    return (await c.query(text, values)).rows as Record<string, unknown>[];
  } finally {
    await c.end();
  }
}

async function canLogin(base: URL, user: string, password: string, db: string): Promise<boolean> {
  const c = new Client({ host: base.hostname, port: Number(base.port), user, password, database: db, ssl: { ca: CA, rejectUnauthorized: true } });
  c.on('error', () => undefined);
  try {
    await c.connect();
    await c.query('SELECT 1');
    return true;
  } catch {
    return false;
  } finally {
    await c.end().catch(() => undefined);
  }
}

const strong = (): string => remember(randomBytes(24).toString('hex'));

interface Fixture {
  db: string;
  admin: string;
  adminPassword: string;
  ownerPassword: string;
}

async function reset(base: URL): Promise<void> {
  const dbs = await sql(base, 'postgres', `SELECT datname FROM pg_catalog.pg_database WHERE datname LIKE 'fbc\\_%'`);
  for (const r of dbs) await sql(base, 'postgres', `DROP DATABASE IF EXISTS ${ident(String(r.datname))} WITH (FORCE)`);
  // DROP OWNED BY first: it also revokes privileges on shared objects (the GRANT SET ON PARAMETER of S1), which DROP ROLE
  // alone refuses with 2BP01.
  const dropRole = async (role: string) => {
    const exists = await sql(base, 'postgres', `SELECT 1 FROM pg_catalog.pg_roles WHERE rolname = $1`, [role]);
    if (exists.length === 0) return;
    await sql(base, 'postgres', `DROP OWNED BY ${ident(role)}`);
    await sql(base, 'postgres', `DROP ROLE ${ident(role)}`);
  };
  for (const role of ['crewflow_worker', 'crewflow_app', 'crewflow', 'rab_app', 'rab_owner', 'rab_secure_owner', 'crewflow_owner']) await dropRole(role);
  const roles = await sql(base, 'postgres', `SELECT rolname FROM pg_catalog.pg_roles WHERE rolname LIKE 'fbc\\_%'`);
  for (const r of roles) await dropRole(String(r.rolname));
}

/** A database owned by a NON-superuser CREATEROLE admin (the shape of a managed provider's admin login). */
async function fixture(base: URL, tag: string): Promise<Fixture> {
  await reset(base);
  const db = `fbc_${tag}_${RUN}`;
  const admin = `fbc_admin_${tag}_${RUN}`;
  const adminPassword = strong();
  await sql(base, 'postgres', `CREATE ROLE ${ident(admin)} LOGIN CREATEROLE`);
  // The admin's password (plain text: the refusing server accepts only that) set by the superuser with logging off.
  await superuserSecret(base, `DO $$ BEGIN EXECUTE pg_catalog.format('ALTER ROLE %I PASSWORD %L', '${admin}', pg_catalog.current_setting('fbc.pw')); END $$`, adminPassword);
  await sql(base, 'postgres', `CREATE DATABASE ${ident(db)} OWNER ${ident(admin)}`);
  return { db, admin, adminPassword, ownerPassword: strong() };
}

/**
 * Runs `statement` as the superuser with the secret in the transaction-local setting fbc.pw, statement logging off for that
 * session: how the harness plays the operator's one SQL-editor step without writing the secret to the server log.
 */
async function superuserSecret(base: URL, statement: string, secret: string, db = 'postgres'): Promise<void> {
  const c = new Client({
    host: base.hostname,
    port: Number(base.port),
    user: decodeURIComponent(base.username),
    password: decodeURIComponent(base.password),
    database: db,
    ssl: { ca: CA, rejectUnauthorized: true },
  });
  await c.connect();
  try {
    await c.query(`SET log_statement = 'none'`);
    await c.query(`SET log_min_duration_statement = -1`);
    await c.query(`SET log_parameter_max_length = 0`);
    await c.query('BEGIN');
    await c.query(`SELECT pg_catalog.set_config('fbc.pw', $1, true) IS NOT NULL`, [secret]);
    await c.query(statement);
    await c.query('COMMIT');
  } finally {
    await c.end();
  }
}

/**
 * Re-review N1 of #259: runs printed statements LITERALLY (the placeholder replaced by `value`), one at a time on one session,
 * as psql sends them. `quiet` turns statement logging off for this session (a superuser only: how a provider with the
 * default log_statement behaves); log_min_error_statement stays at its default, so a failing statement IS quoted in the log.
 * Returns the error message of the first failing statement (after a ROLLBACK), or null.
 */
async function runTyped(base: URL, user: string, password: string, db: string, statements: readonly string[], value: string, quiet: boolean): Promise<string | null> {
  const c = new Client({ host: base.hostname, port: Number(base.port), user, password, database: db, ssl: { ca: CA, rejectUnauthorized: true } });
  await c.connect();
  try {
    if (quiet) {
      await c.query(`SET log_statement = 'none'`);
      await c.query(`SET log_min_duration_statement = -1`);
    }
    for (const st of statements) {
      try {
        await c.query(typed(st, value));
      } catch (error) {
        await c.query('ROLLBACK').catch(() => undefined);
        return error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'error';
      }
    }
    return null;
  } finally {
    await c.end();
  }
}

/**
 * pg_stat_statements rows holding any of `secrets`, read with statement logging off; null when unavailable. `top` counts
 * top-level statements (what the operator sent); `nested` counts statements run INSIDE them (recorded only with
 * pg_stat_statements.track = all). Matching rows are printed with every secret replaced by <value> (the value never).
 */
async function pgssHits(base: URL, secrets: string[]): Promise<{ top: number; nested: number } | null> {
  const c = new Client({ host: base.hostname, port: Number(base.port), user: decodeURIComponent(base.username), password: decodeURIComponent(base.password), database: 'postgres', ssl: { ca: CA, rejectUnauthorized: true } });
  await c.connect();
  try {
    await c.query(`SET log_statement = 'none'`);
    await c.query(`SET log_min_duration_statement = -1`);
    // The statistics are collected from the start (shared_preload_libraries); the view needs the extension in this database.
    try {
      await c.query(`CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS pg_stat_statements`);
    } catch {
      return null;
    }
    const { rows } = await c.query(`SELECT query, toplevel FROM pg_stat_statements`);
    if (rows.length === 0) throw new Failed('pg_stat_statements is empty (cannot prove anything)');
    const hits = rows.filter((r) => secrets.some((x) => x && String(r.query).includes(x)));
    for (const r of hits) {
      let q = String(r.query);
      for (const x of secrets) if (x) q = q.split(x).join('<value>');
      console.log(`[fallback-check] note | pg_stat_statements (${r.toplevel ? 'top-level' : 'nested'}): ${q.replace(/\s+/g, ' ').slice(0, 200)}`);
    }
    return { top: hits.filter((r) => r.toplevel === true).length, nested: hits.filter((r) => r.toplevel !== true).length };
  } finally {
    await c.end();
  }
}

async function ownerCanLoginAttr(base: URL): Promise<boolean | null> {
  const rows = await sql(base, 'postgres', `SELECT rolcanlogin FROM pg_catalog.pg_roles WHERE rolname = 'crewflow_owner'`);
  return rows[0] ? rows[0].rolcanlogin === true : null;
}

async function ownerPasswordState(base: URL): Promise<'missing' | 'none' | 'scram' | 'other'> {
  const rows = await sql(base, 'postgres', `SELECT rolpassword FROM pg_catalog.pg_authid WHERE rolname = 'crewflow_owner'`);
  if (!rows[0]) return 'missing';
  const pw = rows[0].rolpassword;
  if (pw === null || pw === undefined) return 'none';
  return String(pw).startsWith('SCRAM-SHA-256$') ? 'scram' : 'other';
}

/** The simulator's SIGHUP switches (refuse_prehashed.c); the name comes from this fixed list only. */
type SimSwitch = 'refuse_passwordless_role' | 'refuse_plain' | 'refuse_at_statement';
const SIM_SWITCHES: readonly SimSwitch[] = ['refuse_passwordless_role', 'refuse_plain', 'refuse_at_statement'];

async function setSim(name: SimSwitch, on: boolean): Promise<void> {
  if (!SIM_SWITCHES.includes(name)) throw new Error('not a simulator switch');
  await sql(clusters.SIM, 'postgres', `ALTER SYSTEM SET refuse_prehashed.${name} = ${on ? 'on' : 'off'}`);
  await sql(clusters.SIM, 'postgres', `SELECT pg_catalog.pg_reload_conf()`);
  await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 500));
  const shown = await sql(clusters.SIM, 'postgres', `SELECT pg_catalog.current_setting($1) AS v`, [`refuse_prehashed.${name}`]);
  if (shown[0]?.v !== (on ? 'on' : 'off')) throw new Failed(`the simulator switch ${name} did not take effect`);
}

/** Every simulator switch off (the default); run before and after each scenario that turns one on. */
async function simDefaults(): Promise<void> {
  for (const name of SIM_SWITCHES) await setSim(name, false);
}

interface ChildRun {
  code: number | null;
  out: string;
  result: OwnerBootstrapResult | null;
}

function runChild(env: Record<string, string>): Promise<ChildRun> {
  const base: Record<string, string> = {};
  for (const k of ['PATH', 'HOME', 'TMPDIR']) if (process.env[k]) base[k] = process.env[k]!;
  const heap = /^[0-9]{2,5}$/.test(process.env.FBC_CHILD_HEAP ?? '') ? [`--max-old-space-size=${process.env.FBC_CHILD_HEAP}`] : [];
  const argv = [...heap, require.resolve('ts-node/dist/bin.js'), '--transpile-only', '-P', TSCONFIG_APP, ENTRY];
  return new Promise((done) => {
    const child = spawn(process.execPath, argv, { env: { ...base, NODE_ENV: 'test', ...env }, stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'], cwd: REPO_ROOT });
    let out = '';
    child.stdout.on('data', (d) => (out += String(d)));
    child.stderr.on('data', (d) => (out += String(d)));
    child.on('close', (code) => {
      const line = out.split('\n').find((l) => l.startsWith(`${OWNER_BOOTSTRAP_RESULT_PREFIX} `));
      let result: OwnerBootstrapResult | null = null;
      try {
        result = line ? (JSON.parse(line.slice(OWNER_BOOTSTRAP_RESULT_PREFIX.length + 1)) as OwnerBootstrapResult) : null;
      } catch {
        result = null;
      }
      done({ code, out, result });
    });
  });
}

function assertClean(run: ChildRun, extra: string[] = []): void {
  for (const s of [...SECRETS, ...extra]) if (s && run.out.includes(s)) throw new Failed('a secret appeared in the child output (not shown)');
  if (/postgres(ql)?:\/\/[^\s)]*@/i.test(run.out)) throw new Failed('a URL shape appeared in the child output');
  if (run.out.includes('SCRAM-SHA-256$')) throw new Failed('a verifier appeared in the child output');
}

/** The whole log (stdout and stderr) of the simulator's container; never printed. */
function serverLog(container: string | undefined): string {
  if (!container || !/^[a-z0-9_.-]+$/.test(container)) throw new Failed('no container to read the server log from');
  const all = execFileSync('sh', ['-c', `docker logs ${container} 2>&1`], { encoding: 'utf8', maxBuffer: 256 * 1024 * 1024 });
  if (all.length === 0) throw new Failed('the server log is empty (cannot prove anything)');
  return all;
}

/**
 * Security review F5 of #266: `lines` appear in the child output in this ORDER (each after the previous one). On a refusing
 * server: verifierRefused, verifierRetry, then the plain-text line (used / no verified TLS / refused).
 */
function expectInOrder(run: ChildRun, lines: readonly string[], what: string): void {
  let at = -1;
  for (const [i, line] of lines.entries()) {
    const next = run.out.indexOf(line, at + 1);
    expect(next > at, `${what}: fixed line ${i + 1} of ${lines.length} is missing or out of order`);
    at = next;
  }
}

/** The pre-hashed refusals the simulator logged in `tail` (a slice of the server log). */
const prehashedRefusals = (tail: string): number =>
  tail.split('\n').filter((l) => l.includes('simulated refusal: role passwords must be supplied in plain text')).length;

/** Counts lines of a container's log (stdout and stderr) holding a secret; never prints them. */
function logHits(container: string | undefined, secrets: string[]): number {
  return serverLog(container)
    .split('\n')
    .filter((l) => secrets.some((s) => s && l.includes(s))).length;
}

async function ownerState(base: URL): Promise<{ exists: boolean; scram: boolean }> {
  const rows = await sql(base, 'postgres', `SELECT rolpassword FROM pg_catalog.pg_authid WHERE rolname = 'crewflow_owner'`);
  if (!rows[0]) return { exists: false, scram: false };
  return { exists: true, scram: String(rows[0].rolpassword ?? '').startsWith('SCRAM-SHA-256$') };
}

async function created(base: URL, f: Fixture, run: ChildRun, what: string): Promise<void> {
  expect(run.code === 0 && run.result?.outcome === 'created', `${what}: exit ${run.code}, outcome ${run.result?.outcome ?? 'none'} (${run.result?.code ?? ''})`);
  expect((await ownerPasswordState(base)) === 'scram', `${what}: crewflow_owner missing or its password not stored as SCRAM`);
  expect(await canLogin(base, 'crewflow_owner', f.ownerPassword, f.db), `${what}: crewflow_owner cannot log in with its password`);
}


/** The child's environment on the simulator over verified TLS (verify-full + the per-run CA), with `ownerPassword`. */
function simEnv(f: Fixture, ownerPassword: string): Record<string, string> {
  return {
    PG_ADMIN_URL: urlFor(clusters.SIM, f.admin, f.adminPassword, f.db),
    PG_DATABASE_URL: urlFor(clusters.SIM, 'crewflow_owner', ownerPassword, f.db),
    PG_SSL_CA_CERT_PATH: CA_PATH,
  };
}

/**
 * N4 (B) / N5: a plain-text set that FAILS inside its role statement. The verifier is refused inside its own statement
 * (refuse_at_statement, before the catalog row is touched; twice, review F5), so only the plain ALTER ROLE reaches the
 * crewflow_owner row that another session holds: it waits, and lock_timeout (L1: half of deadlock_timeout) cancels it,
 * 55P03. Asserts the clean failure, the cancelled statement in the server log (not vacuous), no FATAL, no log_lock_waits
 * line (review F10) and the role unchanged. Returns the server log written meanwhile.
 */
async function plainSetUnderHeldLock(f: Fixture, next: string, what: string): Promise<string> {
  const container = process.env.FBC_SIM_CONTAINER;
  const before = serverLog(container).length;
  const blocker = new Client({
    host: clusters.SIM.hostname,
    port: Number(clusters.SIM.port),
    user: decodeURIComponent(clusters.SIM.username),
    password: decodeURIComponent(clusters.SIM.password),
    database: 'postgres',
    ssl: { ca: CA, rejectUnauthorized: true },
  });
  await blocker.connect();
  let failed: ChildRun | null = null;
  try {
    await setSim('refuse_at_statement', true);
    await blocker.query('BEGIN');
    // A no-op change that still writes (and so locks) the crewflow_owner row until ROLLBACK.
    await blocker.query('ALTER ROLE crewflow_owner CONNECTION LIMIT -1');
    failed = await runChild({ ...simEnv(f, next), CREWFLOW_ROTATE_APP_PASSWORD: '1' });
  } finally {
    await blocker.query('ROLLBACK').catch(() => undefined);
    await blocker.end().catch(() => undefined);
    await setSim('refuse_at_statement', false);
  }
  if (!failed) throw new Failed(`${what}: the child did not run`);
  expect(failed.code !== 0, `${what}: exit ${failed.code}, expected a failure`);
  expectInOrder(failed, [OWNER_BOOTSTRAP_MESSAGES.verifierRefused('statement', 'XX000'), OWNER_BOOTSTRAP_MESSAGES.verifierRetry], what);
  expect(!failed.out.includes(OWNER_BOOTSTRAP_MESSAGES.plainFallbackUsed('statement', 'XX000')), `${what}: reported a plain-text set`);
  expect(!failed.out.includes(OWNER_BOOTSTRAP_MESSAGES.plainFallbackDeadlockTimeout), `${what}: the plain set was not attempted (deadlock_timeout guard)`);
  expect(failed.out.includes('55P03'), `${what}: the failure is not the lock timeout (${failed.result?.code ?? 'no code'})`);
  assertClean(failed);
  const tail = serverLog(container).slice(before);
  expect(tail.includes('crewflow_owner bootstrap failed (55P03)'), `${what}: the server log does not show the cancelled plain set`);
  // Refused inside the DO block, the simulator's message is caught and re-raised by SQLSTATE: two such lines (review F5).
  const statementRefusals = tail.split('\n').filter((l) => l.includes('crewflow_owner bootstrap failed (XX000)')).length;
  expect(statementRefusals === 2, `${what}: ${statementRefusals} pre-hashed refusal(s) in the server log, expected 2`);
  // The wrong-password probe logs its own FATAL (28P01); a session ended under the plain set (transaction timeout,
  // connection check) must not.
  expect(!/FATAL:\s+terminating connection/.test(tail), `${what}: a session was terminated (FATAL) while the plain set ran`);
  const lockWaitLines = tail.split('\n').filter((l) => l.includes('still waiting for')).length;
  expect(lockWaitLines === 0, `${what}: ${lockWaitLines} log_lock_waits line(s) while the plain set waited`);
  expect(await canLogin(clusters.SIM, 'crewflow_owner', f.ownerPassword, f.db), `${what}: the original password no longer logs in`);
  expect(!(await canLogin(clusters.SIM, 'crewflow_owner', next, f.db)), `${what}: the failed value logs in`);
  expect(logHits(container, [f.ownerPassword, next]) === 0, `${what}: a crewflow_owner password appears in the server log`);
  return tail;
}

